# Line ending policy.
#
# Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites line endings on
# checkout. For the shell scripts that is not a style preference — it is a build
# failure: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` script with CRLF endings dies on Linux and macOS
# with
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# because the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named `bash\r`. GitHub
# Actions runs on Linux and macOS, so without this file the bootstrap script would
# never execute there.
#
# `text eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on every platform.

# Shell scripts — must be LF or they cannot be executed.
*.sh          text eol=lf

# Python — a CRLF shebang breaks the same way.
*.py          text eol=lf

# Sources: LF everywhere for consistent diffs across platforms.
*.swift       text eol=lf
*.h           text eol=lf
*.m           text eol=lf
*.mm          text eol=lf
*.c           text eol=lf

# Configuration and docs.
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.entitlements text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.ipa         binary
*.dylib       binary
*.jar         binary
*.zip         binary
*.tar.xz      binary
*.png         binary
*.ttf         binary
